   "title": "Approved Cluster Courses",
   "section": "Cluster Courses",
   "notes": "Two of the best reasons to study statistics are the immense variety of important and exciting real-world questions we can answer through careful data analysis, as well as the broad range of technical fields with close connections to statistics. No major is complete without encountering the fields that interface closely with statistics. … (see the catalog for the rest)\nOf the three applied cluster courses required for the major, at least two must be approved courses from the same department. This is not an exhaustive list.\n- Only one course may be selected from ECON 136, ENGIN 120 and UGBA 103.\n- If Math 110 or H110 has been used to satisfy math prerequisite requirement, course cannot be used for applied cluster.\n- Math 170 cannot be combined with either IEOR 160 or IEOR 162. … (see the catalog for the rest)",
